{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts","id":1016834,"title":"How easy is it to learn gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T17:39:16-08:00","id":1016834,"title":"How easy is it to learn gifts","content":"I've been playing Werewolf for about 3 years now, the first 2 as a player, the next year as an ST. However, a lot of what I did was based on how our old ST ran things, and as I started reading more and more of the book, I realized there was a lot of things we did wrong. One of them I'm not so sure about though, is learning gifts. There's a small section before the gifts that says:<br /> <br /> &quot;Most often, a werewolf must either petition a particular spirit to teach her its powers or ask an elder to summon that spirit on their behalf. Traditionally, the Garou first travels to a caern with a power level equal to or greater than the desired Gift to petition the spirit personally - to do otherwise is to defy tradition, which risks incurring the wrath of the spirit. But as more caerns fall to the talons of the Wyrm, many Garou are forced to make do with whatever places of power they can find, or even summon spirits outside of caerns completely.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the game in which I was a player, we just summoned spirits willy nilly and had them teach us where ever. Our Theurge had the Rite of Spirit Summoning, and we would just summon whatever we needed, and with a good enough roll, the chart always ended up on them coming in &quot;Friendly&quot;. However, reading the passage makes it sound like learning Gifts is not that simple. I'm struggling with a few things about it though. It says Garou would travel to a caern to address the spirit personally. Does that mean finding one with a caern totem that matches? Or just finding a caern and asking any spirit of the kind you need that resides there?<br /> <br /> My old ST also made it seem like most Garou had a ton of Gifts. In his mind, if you're not leaving Rank 1 with 9+ Gifts, you're not doing it right. So how does everyone else run learning Gifts in their games, and how many do people tend to end up with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:59:55-08:00","id":1016841,"title":"","content":"Unless your pack did something to piss off a particular type of spirit, I'd divide it based on whether the gift is in or out of tribe/auspice/breed for the character. If it is out of breed, I may have the spirit require a favor from the character. If say a Bone Gnawer wants a gift from Falcon or something, the favor may be more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T20:58:21-08:00","id":1016898,"title":"","content":"I don't think most players and STs make it that difficult. I mentioned on a post here several months ago that learning Gifts required you to summon a spirit at the same the Caern level as the Gift you want to learn (or higher), and everyone else who posted asked, &quot;Where did you read that?&quot; When I pointed out it's been the language in every core book edition, all acted surprised. Most people just want to spend the XP and move on.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles though, I follow that. Proper petitioning of the spirit is important. And at higher Gift levels, it may require you to visit other caerns. I've always been find with that because the early Rage books made it seem like that the default setting of any chronicle needed to include multiple caerns of various levels. and that visiting other caerns were routine. Of course, once you properly propitiate the spirit - the actual learning of the Gift is automatic.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you eschew the proper protocols, you can still learn Gifts or even be taught by Garou instead of spirits. Of course if you do that you gain notoriety in the spirit world.<br /> <br /> The question about how many Gifts a Garou should have really depends on each chronicle. Different people are going to have different ideas about what is right. 9 Gifts when turn rank 2 seems way too high to me, but I think a lot of people have fun with those kind of high XP games. I'd expect more between 4-6 Gifts when you reach rank 2. I tend to like games that are more down to level than epic fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:27:45-08:00","id":1016915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts#post1016834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the game in which I was a player, we just summoned spirits willy nilly and had them teach us where ever. Our Theurge had the Rite of Spirit Summoning, and we would just summon whatever we needed, and with a good enough roll, the chart always ended up on them coming in &quot;Friendly&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a Spirit show up friendly is great. That doesn't mean that they are going to (<i>or even can</i>) defy tradition. It is understood that the Garou asking for something is going to bargain for that thing. So offerings are prepared in advance to thank the Spirit for arriving, and then the Garou negotiate what services they will provide in payment for the Spirit teaching them the Gift (Chiminage). This has always been my experience in Werewolf. So while the XP cost is relatively low, the in game role playing cost tends to be more in depth. And the higher the Rank Gift, the more involved the Chiminage is going to be.<br /> And again, having a spirit like you isn't enough to overturn tens of thousands (or more) of years of tradition. In general, Spirits cannot defy their nature. And Pacts are ingrained in their nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts#post1016834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, reading the passage makes it sound like learning Gifts is not that simple. I'm struggling with a few things about it though. It says Garou would travel to a caern to address the spirit personally. Does that mean finding one with a caern totem that matches? Or just finding a caern and asking any spirit of the kind you need that resides there?</div> </div> </div> </div>So my interpretation on the Caern level must equal the Gift level thing is it is disrespectful to summon a more powerful Spirit (the kind that can or is going to teach higher rank Gifts) to lower level Caerns. And respect is huge with spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts#post1016834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My old ST also made it seem like most Garou had a ton of Gifts. In his mind, if you're not leaving Rank 1 with 9+ Gifts, you're not doing it right. So how does everyone else run learning Gifts in their games, and how many do people tend to end up with?</div> </div> </div> </div> I tend to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> on this one for number of Gifts going into Rank 2. 4-6 sounds about normal from my experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1016898#post1016898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think most players and STs make it that difficult. I mentioned on a post here several months ago that learning Gifts required you to summon a spirit at the same the Caern level as the Gift you want to learn (or higher), and everyone else who posted asked, &quot;Where did you read that?&quot; When I pointed out it's been the language in every core book edition, all acted surprised. Most people just want to spend the XP and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that thread. It's a good bit of information to remember.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:48:11-08:00","id":1016919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts#post1016834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a small section before the gifts that says:</div> </div> </div> </div>It also says, &quot;Such slighted spirits often demand recompense or service before consenting to share their blessings.&quot;<br /> <br /> So the &quot;have to go to a high Ranked Caern part,&quot; can simply replaced by &quot;doing more chiminage for the spirit to get the Gift,&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> I don't think your group was doing it wrong necessarily. The point for the books is that learning Gifts has a significant in-character opportunity cost involved with it. Traveling to other Caerns is the &quot;simple&quot; method, but that means leaving your home territory less protected, and dealing with the other Caern's Garou (or others) to get access. If you want to stay focused on a single location, you can summon away, but then there's the cost of needing to pay much higher chiminage each time. If you can't summon, then you have to Umbral quest on top of the increased chiminage for not going to a Caern.<br /> <br /> The books add a lot of exceptions to this, probably to avoid locking the game into either happening at Rank 5 Caerns, or being a high travel game. You pick the option that works best for the kind of story you want to go with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It says Garou would travel to a caern to address the spirit personally. Does that mean finding one with a caern totem that matches? Or just finding a caern and asking any spirit of the kind you need that resides there? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really specify. I've always gone with the later option though, simply because the first makes learning Gifts obnoxiously hard simply by the shear number of different Caerns you'd need to have to visit to cover your bases (and various spirits that generally don't act as Caern Totems like Ancestor spirits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My old ST also made it seem like most Garou had a ton of Gifts. In his mind, if you're not leaving Rank 1 with 9+ Gifts, you're not doing it right. So how does everyone else run learning Gifts in their games, and how many do people tend to end up with? </div> </div> </div>It depends a lot on the ST. Part of the problem is that there's a big disconnect in the books. The books tend to present Gifts as relatively rare. Most high level canon NPCs with stats have between 9 and 12 Gifts total across all the Ranks they have access too, and almost never have out-of-splat Gifts. Meanwhile Gifts are extremely cheap for the XP, and are generally better than most other XP investments you could make for the same XP. So if you have access to a Gift that suits your character, there's almost never an in-character reason or and out-of-character reason to not take it. So IME, PC Garou tend to have way, way more Gifts than the books seem to think they're going to. Even in game where the ST has been fairly restrictive with learning Gifts, having 6-9 Rank 1 Gifts was not uncommon.<br /> <br /> The only time I see Gift selections that look more like the characters in the books are games that tend to ramp up Renown and Rank fairly quickly (because you'll take higher Rank Gifts if you can most of the time); but then the other traits don't tend to line up instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:54:52-08:00","id":1016922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1016915#post1016915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that thread. It's a good bit of information to remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! We had a very good, productive dialogue on that. Thanks very much. I found the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938575-where-should-be-the-rank-5-caerns\">original thread</a> in case it helps the original poster at all. Even the dissenting posts were well made.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:07:08-08:00","id":1016988,"title":"","content":"Lots of great answers in here. Thanks for the information!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:17:24-08:00","id":1017020,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I generally think that most Garou are going to be spending around 40% of their XP on Gifts. A Rank 5 Garou with 500 XP should have 200 XP in Gifts. As mentioned before, it just makes more sense to invest more XP in Gifts than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:10:35-08:00","id":1017045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1017020#post1017020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I generally think that most Garou are going to be spending around 40% of their XP on Gifts. A Rank 5 Garou with 500 XP should have 200 XP in Gifts. As mentioned before, it just makes more sense to invest more XP in Gifts than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I'd just handwave any necessary spirit interaction for in-auspice/tribe/breed gifts. You spend XP and talked to the spirit during down time. <br /> <br /> If you want something outside your usual gift category, then you will have to rp talking to the spirit. Maybe do a small favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:58:31-08:00","id":1017122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1017045#post1017045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd just handwave any necessary spirit interaction for in-auspice/tribe/breed gifts. You spend XP and talked to the spirit during down time.<br /> <br /> If you want something outside your usual gift category, then you will have to rp talking to the spirit. Maybe do a small favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how we do it in the Werewolf LARP I play in.<br /> <br /> Basic (Rank 1+2) In-BAT Gifts from LOTW, PGtG, BoA, or the Tribebook can be purchased during Downtime freely. Otherwise, all Gifts require a Scene. Zero of my current PCs Gifts are out-of-BAT, but that has more to do with his Pack makeup than anything else, because we have a member of every Auspice and they mostly show up pretty regularly. In the previous game I played long in, my Pack had been just two characters for so long, everyone kept forgetting that Sense Wyrm wasn't in-BAT for Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> My PC is just about ready to Challenge for Athro and has 23 Gifts, 5 of which are Rank 3/4.<br /> When he Challenged for Adren, he had 14 Gifts, all of which were Rank 1/2.<br /> When he Challenged for Fostern, he had 9 Gifts, all of which were Rank 1/2.<br /> <br /> It's important to note, however, that things in MET are a little different. You quickly run out of things to spend XP on other than Magical Powers and the Abilities associated with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:15:15-08:00","id":1017162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1017045#post1017045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd just handwave any necessary spirit interaction for in-auspice/tribe/breed gifts. You spend XP and talked to the spirit during down time.<br /> <br /> If you want something outside your usual gift category, then you will have to rp talking to the spirit. Maybe do a small favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously whatever works for your group/game is what's important.<br /> <br /> That being said, personally I think this approach takes away a lot from a Werewolf (or other Fera) game. The &quot;small favors&quot; that you do for Gifts acts as a counterweight for the low-ish XP cost. At higher ranks, I've hand waived the Chiminages for lower Rank Gifts, but when the characters are lower Rank it's fun (imo) to role play through the bargaining. Since the characters (and sometimes the Players) aren't familiar with the ins and outs of Spirit interaction at that point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:18:54-08:00","id":1017164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1017162#post1017162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously whatever works for your group/game is what's important.<br /> <br /> That being said, personally I think this approach takes away a lot from a Werewolf (or other Fera) game. The &quot;small favors&quot; that you do for Gifts acts as a counterweight for the low-ish XP cost. At higher ranks, I've hand waived the Chiminages for lower Rank Gifts, but when the characters are lower Rank it's fun (imo) to role play through the bargaining. Since the characters (and sometimes the Players) aren't familiar with the ins and outs of Spirit interaction at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was in a MET Laws of the Wild game a long time ago. We had about 15 -20 players and only three narrators. I imagine they ran it this way to free up narrators for plot related scenes. <br /> <br /> I think we ran scenes for higher level gifts. Or maybe it was when my Homid Glasswalker Ragabash learned Sense Wyrm. It's been a while, so I don't remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:27:17-08:00","id":1017172,"title":"","content":"That makes more sense. Either way, I was trying to avoid being critical of other people's playstyles. There is no correct way to play pretend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:35:09-08:00","id":1017181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1016834-how-easy-is-it-to-learn-gifts?p=1017172#post1017172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes more sense. Either way, I was trying to avoid being critical of other people's playstyles. There is no correct way to play pretend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very true.<br /> <br /> It was a City Sept where there was only one Bone Gnawer and Three Glasswalker PCs in the entire game. I remember the first game where my Glasswalker gun smuggler gleefully sold a Fianna a gun. It was a strange game, but good times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}